# Frontend conventions

- Function components only, with one default-exported component per file. Hooks must follow the rules of hooks and list complete effect dependencies.
- Pages go in `src/pages/` and shared UI goes in `src/components/`.
- Register routes in `src/router.tsx` as children of `Layout` (React Router data mode, imported from `react-router`). Keep the `*` catch-all route last. Add nav links in `src/components/Layout.tsx`.
- Make HTTP calls through the shared axios instance in `src/api.ts`. Use paths relative to `/api`; never hardcode the backend host. Vite proxies `/api` to the backend in dev.

```tsx
// Bad
fetch('http://localhost:3001/api/health')

// Good
import { api } from '../api'
api.get<{ status: string }>('/health')
```

- Type API responses with the generic on `api.get<T>()` etc. instead of casting.
- Handle the loading and error states for every request (see `src/pages/HomePage.tsx`).
- Give list items a stable `key` (not the array index when items can reorder).
